	"department": "ART",
	"description": [
		"This course examines the art of Europe created between 1300 and 1650, a time when Europe's colonial and economic power in the world was growing. Through in-depth analysis of several case studies, the course considers the power that objects had to create and perpetuate concepts of race, gender, and colonial expansion in the period."
